WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.450
- There really are no words

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.280
that I have for our next guest,

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.870
except to say that

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.090
she's not just a guest,

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.270
she's a woman

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.480
who is showing up for a friend,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.890
me.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.940
we've actually known
each other since we were,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.773
oh my gosh,

00:00:15.773 --> 00:00:17.340
14?

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.570
We've been pregnant together,

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.650
and at weddings

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.650
and she's someone that I
deeply, deeply, deeply respect.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.910
And so do you.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.310
She has a book club.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.980
She's created job opportunities

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.710
in the Hollywood industry
that are unprecedented.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.360
She has a production company,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.460
Hello Sunshine.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.620
She's someone who's a
true Maven and a pioneer.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.453
So

00:00:42.453 --> 00:00:44.070
ladies and gentlemen, without further ado,

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.736
Reese Witherspoon.

00:00:45.736 --> 00:00:47.922
(people applauding)

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:49.514
- Hi?

00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:50.470
Hi friend?

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:51.900
- Oh my goodness.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.573
Thank you so much for
christening the show.

00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:57.940
(Drew laughs)

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.300
- I am so excited, Drew.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.063
When I heard you were doing a show,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:04.743
I said,

00:01:04.743 --> 00:01:05.576
this is the perfect person,

00:01:05.576 --> 00:01:08.110
because whenever you were on a TV show,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.010
I literally stopped whenever I'm doing,

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:10.850
just to watch you,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.970
because you bring me so much joy.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.560
- You are someone

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.140
that I feel like is very emblematic

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.460
of what I would like to
try to do with the show.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.880
You're interested in so
many different things,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.670
and a show like this as an opportunity

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.940
for me to take all of those interests

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.490
and put them in a piggy bank

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.563
and break it on the floor every day.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.683
- That's such a good
metaphor, I love that.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.054
Well, we've known each
other for so long, right?

00:01:38.054 --> 00:01:38.887
I think...

00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:39.970
- How old were we Reese?

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.440
I thought we were 13

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.130
and then I realized you
had done "Man on the Moon".

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.440
So you must've been 14.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.950
- I was 14 years old.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.817
I was completely obsessed with you

00:01:49.817 --> 00:01:53.400
and you had no idea that
I was like your super fan.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.770
I had read your book.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.850
I had pictures of you on my wall.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.460
You were like my childhood acting idle,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.457
and you came up to me in
a restaurant and you said,

00:02:01.457 --> 00:02:04.100
"I saw you in a movie and
you were so wonderful."

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:04.933
And do you know,

00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:08.810
it changed my whole perspective on,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.920
like you were one of the first
people who ever supported me

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.010
and showed me, it doesn't
have to be competitive,

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.210
that creativity is infinite.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.560
And if we can collaborate,

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.060
as women together,

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.930
we can accomplish so much more.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.590
- I Marvel at the opportunities

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.650
that you give to women.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.483
And,

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:34.160
I think there's sometimes
a fear in general

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.210
that if you lift someone else up,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.250
you like, will either
go down or not be seen.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.490
And I think,

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.890
and you obviously are the symbol of this,

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.500
that when you lift someone else up,

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.760
you go up with them

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.940
and there's enough light and creativity

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.580
and room for everyone.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.650
But,

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.390
you not only lift people up
and shine a light on them,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:00.500
but you give them opportunities
that are very rare.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.740
And I am so impressed
with what you are doing.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.910
It's just incredible.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.930
- Well, thank you for saying that.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.150
I have gotten so much
inspiration from so many women

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.510
who are doing work like this,

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.343
including, you know,

00:03:15.343 --> 00:03:17.890
Ava DuVernay, and Lina Wert

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:18.723
and yourself.

00:03:18.723 --> 00:03:20.670
When you created flower films,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.047
that gave me courage to say,

00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:24.130
"Hey, I could have a company too."

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:26.520
And I'll never forget when
you called me on the phone

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.353
and I said,

00:03:27.353 --> 00:03:30.140
"Drew, I love that you're
creating female superheroes

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.530
because I have a little girl in the car",

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.300
and my daughter was young then.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.550
And I said, "you don't understand,

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.550
there's no female superheroes."

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.570
That was something that
was so important to you,

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:45.030
but it gave me courage to
start my company and say,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.610
you know, when we see
systems that are broken,

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:49.720
right?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.380
Whatever system you work in,

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.830
it could be your school district,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.070
it could be your community,

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.340
your city, government.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.270
We looked at our
Hollywood system and said,

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.810
you know, not good enough.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.060
There's not enough projects for women,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.980
there's not enough female directors,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.600
there's not enough people of color writing

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.340
and getting show running-opportunities.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.130
And I think that feeling

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.660
that you can take control of your life

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.660
and that everyone has the
ability to tell their own story.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.480
I think we're going through,

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.690
obviously,

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.730
some really difficult times,

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.600
but I'm such an optimist.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.520
I'm always like there's
such rebirth and regrowth

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.250
that comes out of that
kind of pain and struggle.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.250
- When I called you that day,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.090
it scared me, it intimidated me.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.960
You had these two young kids in the back

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.630
and I thought, God, I'm
so far away from that.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.122
Like,

00:04:47.122 --> 00:04:50.560
I would be so scared if
somebody put two young kids

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.057
in the back of my car and said,

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:54.290
"Just go and take them and feed them",

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.123
you know,

00:04:55.123 --> 00:04:56.890
it cut to like years later,

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.220
the full circle story of irony is

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.810
we were both pregnant
together at my wedding

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.780
with like bumping bellies,

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.720
the only two sober chicks there

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.360
and,

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.740
I was so amazed by you
being this young mother

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.373
who was able to take all that on.

00:05:15.373 --> 00:05:16.323
And,

00:05:16.323 --> 00:05:17.156
did you,

00:05:17.156 --> 00:05:19.670
how did you balance work and
motherhood at that point?

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.900
Cause I was just trying to balance work,

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.733
and

00:05:22.733 --> 00:05:24.680
how did you do both?

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.280
Yeah. Well, to be completely candid,

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.460
I was terrified too.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.120
I got pregnant when I was 22 years old

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:37.000
and I didn't know how to
balance work and motherhood.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.420
And we just,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.280
you just do it, you know.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.940
I didn't know if I was going
to have steady work too,

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.070
I wasn't a popular,

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.810
like, I made movies, but I hadn't,

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:47.643
you know,

00:05:47.643 --> 00:05:51.950
established myself as
someone who could demand that

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.300
it shoot close to my kids' school or,

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.553
you know,

00:05:55.553 --> 00:05:59.550
I didn't have any real power
leverage within my industry.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:00.383
So

00:06:00.383 --> 00:06:02.160
I think I was just like every other mom

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.190
trying to figure it out,

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:05.430
and dad out there, and
partner, and grandparent,

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.950
who's raising a child.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.270
There's a lot of,

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.630
first of all, compromise.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:10.990
You take the food out of your mouth,

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.460
the clothes off your back,

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.600
the sleep out of your life.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.270
Like, every bit of it,

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.550
every bit of that
sacrifice is truly worth it

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.200
because you feel like,

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.860
that's what makes me wake up on a Sunday

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.450
is not a

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.283
movies,

00:06:26.283 --> 00:06:27.116
is not my job.

00:06:27.116 --> 00:06:28.476
Is my kids.

00:06:28.476 --> 00:06:31.059
(upbeat music)

